00:19:08,119 --> 00:19:14,119
What do you think of the 60% for instance in terms of GDP growth?
你如何看待例如占GDP增长60%这一数据？

316
00:19:14,119 --> 00:19:20,119
Service sector contributed for 60% of China's GDP growth. How significant is that?
服务业贡献了中国GDP增长的60%，这有多重要？

317
00:19:20,119 --> 00:19:34,119
This is also very significant. I think it accounts for 60% of the GDP growth, which means that it already becomes the majority, the major part of the growth, the major source of growth.
这同样非常重要。我认为它占GDP增长的60%，意味着它已经成为增长的主要部分，即主要增长来源。

318
00:19:34,119 --> 00:19:44,119
I think this portion will become larger in the future. In particular, in China, high value added service as well as manufacturing service, etc.
我认为这一比例在未来会更大。特别是在中国，高附加值服务业以及制造业服务等领域。

319
00:19:44,119 --> 00:19:49,119
A lot of new service products will emerge in the future.
未来将会涌现出许多新的服务产品。

320
00:19:49,119 --> 00:19:59,119
How about travel? I mean, we are seeing every year even more the travel rush during big holidays such as the May Day holiday.
旅游业怎么样？我是说，我们每年都能看到，即使在像五一假期这样的大节假日期间，旅游热潮也一年比一年更甚。

321
00:19:59,119 --> 00:20:03,119
What trends are forming there?
那里正在形成哪些趋势？

322
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:14,119
Traveling is certainly a very big demand of the service sector. In old times people looked at the price and location.
旅游业无疑是服务业中一个非常大的需求。过去人们主要看价格和位置。

323
00:20:14,119 --> 00:20:22,119
But in the future, I think people will look at better services in traveling.
但未来，我认为人们会追求更好的旅游服务。

324
00:20:22,119 --> 00:20:33,119
For example, they will probably use some AI tools to identify the best itinerary and to get the best place for shopping.
例如，他们可能会使用一些人工智能工具来识别最佳行程，并找到最佳的购物地点。

325
00:20:33,119 --> 00:20:41,119
And to identify the place that there are no crowds, etc. to improve the quality of the traveling.
以及识别那些没有人群拥挤的地方，等等，以提升旅游质量。

326
00:20:41,119 --> 00:20:47,119
Also, they will probably identify the local best restaurants, etc.
此外，他们可能还会识别当地最好的餐厅等。

327
00:20:47,119 --> 00:20:52,119
I think the quality and experience will be much improved in the future.
我认为未来质量和体验会有很大的提升。

328
00:20:52,119 --> 00:21:06,119
As people become more sophisticated in terms of consuming services, which brings us to the nation's drive to meet these kinds of demands, these kinds of growing needs.
随着人们在消费服务方面变得更加成熟，这也促使国家去满足这些需求，这些不断增长的需求。

329
00:21:06,119 --> 00:21:14,119
I was talking about the size of China's service sector being about US$12 trillion for last year.
我刚才提到，去年中国服务业的规模约为12万亿美元。

330
00:21:14,119 --> 00:21:23,119
China has this planning system, so we have laid out the next five-year plan, which is from 2025 to 2030.
中国有规划体系，因此我们制定了下一个五年计划，即2025年至2030年。

331
00:21:23,119 --> 00:21:33,119
It is expected that the service sector will grow to be as strong as US$15 trillion, that's US$100 trillion yuan.
预计服务业将增长至15万亿美元，也就是100万亿元人民币。

332
00:21:33,119 --> 00:21:38,119
How does China have the confidence that it can achieve this goal?
中国凭什么有信心实现这一目标？

333
00:21:38,119 --> 00:21:44,119
And what will be the key drivers behind this growth?
推动这一增长的关键因素是什么？

334
00:21:44,119 --> 00:21:51,119
First of all, from $12 trillion to $15 trillion in five years is not a big deal for China.
首先，从12万亿美元增长到15万亿美元，五年时间对中国来说并不难。

335
00:21:51,119 --> 00:21:57,119
It only takes like 4-5% growth per year, so we will achieve that goal.
每年只需4%到5%的增长，我们就能实现这一目标。

336
00:21:57,119 --> 00:22:10,119
Second, I think with the technology development, in particular with data technology and AI technology, I think we will create a lot of new models for service in China.
其次，我认为随着技术的发展，特别是数据技术和人工智能技术，我们在中国将创造许多新的服务模式。

337
00:22:10,119 --> 00:22:16,119
And also, green service is also a big part of this service sector growth as well.
此外，绿色服务也是这一服务业增长的重要组成部分。

338
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:26,119
In China, also, we need a lot of high-value added service, high-quality service, being healthcare and senior care.
在中国，我们还需要大量高附加值的服务，高质量的服务，比如医疗保健和老年护理。

339
00:22:26,119 --> 00:22:34,119
In traveling, you just mentioned, we do need a lot of high-value added service as well.
在你刚才提到的旅游业中，我们同样需要大量高附加值的服务。

340
00:22:34,119 --> 00:22:43,119
So there's a lot of space to grow, new products, new services, the combination of service and products, the combination of manufacturing services,
因此，增长空间很大，包括新产品、新服务、服务与产品的结合、制造业与服务的结合，

341
00:22:43,119 --> 00:22:50,119
as well as AI applications, generating new business models in the service sector.
以及人工智能应用，在服务领域催生新的商业模式。

342
00:22:50,119 --> 00:22:58,119
There's too much space to grow. I think this is a very conservative estimate to grow to $15 billion.
增长空间太大了。我认为增长到150亿美元是一个非常保守的估计。

343
00:22:58,119 --> 00:23:00,119
I think it could be $20 billion.
我觉得可能是200亿美元。

344
00:23:00,119 --> 00:23:01,619
Wow.
哇。

345
00:23:01,119 --> 00:23:03,119
Well, if we do the right thing.
嗯，如果我们做对的话。

346
00:23:03,119 --> 00:23:04,619
Do the right thing.
做对的话。

347
00:23:04,119 --> 00:23:13,119
Well, as you mentioned, new things will emerge, for instance, new models and new consumption patterns.
嗯，正如你提到的，会出现新事物，例如新模型和新的消费模式。

348
00:23:13,119 --> 00:23:21,119
What could be some of the new consumption models and service scenarios that we can expect to emerge?
我们可以预期会出现哪些新的消费模式和服务场景？

349
00:23:21,119 --> 00:23:26,119
And how is that going to change people's way of leading their lives?
这将如何改变人们的生活方式？

350
00:23:26,119 --> 00:23:31,119
There are just many things that could occur in the near future.
在不久的将来，可能会发生很多事情。

351
00:23:31,119 --> 00:23:41,119
For example, the AI application in people's daily life, we could use the AI agent to do the planning for our traveling,
例如，人工智能在日常生活中的应用，我们可以使用AI智能体来规划我们的旅行，

352
00:23:41,119 --> 00:23:48,119
and we use the AI for work to design the working schedule.
并使用人工智能来设计工作日程。

353
00:23:48,119 --> 00:23:54,119
Also, there will be integration of manufacturing and services.
此外，制造业和服务业将会融合。

354
00:23:54,119 --> 00:24:00,119
First of all, a lot of products will be sold along with a lot of service products.
首先，许多产品将伴随着大量的服务产品一起销售。

355
00:24:00,119 --> 00:24:10,119
For example, if you buy a car, then it could be like an AMAP tool on it, and also connecting to a lot of other services.
例如，如果你买一辆车，它可能就像上面装了一个高德地图工具，并且连接到许多其他服务。

356
00:24:10,119 --> 00:24:16,119
If you buy a cell phone, it will come with other products, many many service products as well.
如果你买一部手机，它会附带其他产品，以及许多许多服务产品。

357
00:24:16,119 --> 00:24:22,119
Secondly, I think in the manufacturing sector, we also need production service,
其次，我认为在制造业，我们也需要生产性服务，

358
00:24:22,119 --> 00:24:29,119
which means we use the tools to improve efficiency in manufacturing,
这意味着我们使用工具来提高制造业的效率，

359
00:24:29,119 --> 00:24:39,119
like planning, like scheduling logistics, like legal services, like strategy consulting.
比如规划，比如物流调度，比如法律服务，比如战略咨询。

360
00:24:39,119 --> 00:24:40,619
Aftersale.
售后。

361
00:24:40,119 --> 00:24:46,119
Aftersale services, like compliance services, like risk management.
售后服务，比如合规服务，比如风险管理。

362
00:24:46,119 --> 00:24:53,119
All these types of services for manufacturing for the goods production is also a big part of this.
这些面向制造业和商品生产的服务也是其中重要的一部分。

363
00:24:53,119 --> 00:25:00,119
What kind of new scenarios are being created with the introduction of AI?
随着人工智能的引入，正在创造哪些新场景？

364
00:25:00,119 --> 00:25:08,119
For instance, I was listening to Mr. Lee Gung from AMAP to talk about the introduction of AI technology into AMAP,
例如，我听了高德地图的李刚先生谈论将人工智能技术引入高德地图，

365
00:25:08,119 --> 00:25:14,119
so that people have greater experience. For instance, the Flying Street View feature of the map.
以便人们获得更好的体验。比如地图的飞行街景功能。

366
00:25:14,119 --> 00:25:21,119
How are new scenarios being created, and what impact could this have?
新场景是如何被创造的，这可能带来什么影响？

367
00:25:21,119 --> 00:25:25,119
I think the technology just makes our lives much more colorful.
我认为技术只是让我们的生活变得更加丰富多彩。

368
00:25:25,119 --> 00:25:30,119
Originally, for example, the AMAP would just give you the route to a destiny,
起初，例如，高德地图只会给你一条到目的地的路线，

369
00:25:30,119 --> 00:25:33,119
to a destiny, give you the best route for now.
到目的地，给你当前最佳的路线。

370
00:25:33,119 --> 00:25:39,119
But now, it used to be just a reactive. You give the AMAP an order, they would give you an answer.
但现在，过去它只是被动的。你给高德地图一个指令，它会给你一个答案。

371
00:25:39,119 --> 00:25:43,119
But in the future, it will be much more proactive and immersive.
但在未来，它将变得更加主动和沉浸式。

372
00:25:43,119 --> 00:25:48,119
He could automatically provide other products and services for the suggestion,
它可以自动提供其他产品和服务的建议，

373
00:25:48,119 --> 00:25:55,119
and also, it could make your experience much, much more immersive, like you really in it.
而且，它可以让你的体验变得更加、更加沉浸式，就像你真的身在其中一样。

374
00:25:55,119 --> 00:25:59,119
This is, I think, a big change of our life.
我认为，这是我们生活的一个巨大变化。

375
00:25:59,119 --> 00:26:06,119
What kind of opportunities is this AI plus services creating for foreign businesses?
这种“人工智能+服务”为外国企业创造了什么样的机会？

376
00:26:06,119 --> 00:26:13,119
I understand the investment in high-tech sector, especially for foreign direct investment,
我了解到，高科技领域的投资，特别是外商直接投资，

377
00:26:13,119 --> 00:26:17,119
really shot up 30% in the first quarter of this year.
今年第一季度真的猛增了30%。

378
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:22,119
So, what opportunities lie in AI plus services for foreign businesses?
那么，“人工智能+服务”为外国企业带来了哪些机遇？

379
00:26:22,119 --> 00:26:26,119
I think there's just a lot of opportunities for foreign investors as well.
我认为，外国投资者也有很多机会。

380
00:26:26,119 --> 00:26:30,119
For example, as I mentioned, there's a high-value added service.
例如，正如我提到的，有高附加值的服务。

381
00:26:30,119 --> 00:26:34,119
In China, the old model is very low-priced, long hours.
在中国，旧模式的特点是价格低廉、工时漫长。

382
00:26:34,119 --> 00:26:35,619
Cheap labor?
廉价劳动力？

383
00:26:35,119 --> 00:26:36,619
Cheap labor.
廉价劳动力。

384
00:26:36,119 --> 00:26:44,119
But now, with the assistance of AI, high-quality services will become much more accessible in China.
但现在，借助人工智能，在中国，高质量的服务将变得更加普及。

385
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:48,119
So, it certainly improved the quality of this kind of trade services.
所以，它确实提高了这类贸易服务的质量。

386
00:26:48,119 --> 00:26:53,119
What kind of risks do you think there may be? And what kind of bottlenecks?
你认为可能存在哪些风险？以及哪些瓶颈？

387
00:26:54,119 --> 00:27:01,119
The biggest risk is probably the governance of new technology.
最大的风险可能是新技术的治理。

388
00:27:01,119 --> 00:27:10,119
Technology is neutral. It could bring good things and also equally likely bring bad things.
技术是中性的。它既可能带来好事，也同样可能带来坏事。

389
00:27:10,119 --> 00:27:14,119
So, for example, people use AI to improve their quality.
例如，人们利用人工智能来提高他们的质量。

390
00:27:14,119 --> 00:27:22,119
Certainly, we now see a lot of people use AI tool to cheat as well.
当然，我们现在也看到很多人利用人工智能工具作弊。

391
00:27:22,119 --> 00:27:26,119
And sometimes our privacy is not well protected.
而且，有时候我们的隐私没有得到很好的保护。

392
00:27:26,119 --> 00:27:30,119
So, this could be a big concern as well.
所以，这也是一个很大的担忧。

393
00:27:30,119 --> 00:27:33,119
What's China's approach to addressing these bottlenecks?
中国应对这些瓶颈的方法是什么？

394
00:27:33,119 --> 00:27:44,119
I think China should improve the legislation in this area for the governance in AI.
我认为中国应该完善该领域的立法，以加强对人工智能的治理。

395
00:27:44,119 --> 00:27:47,119
Also, try to break this local protectionism.
此外，还要努力打破地方保护主义。

396
00:27:47,119 --> 00:27:54,119
Also, I think training workforce is important because not only we need people to have the new demand,
另外，我认为培训劳动力也很重要，因为我们不仅需要人们了解新的需求，

397
00:27:54,119 --> 00:27:58,119
know the new demand, but also we need people who can provide these services.
了解新的需求，还需要能够提供服务的人才。

398
00:27:58,119 --> 00:28:04,119
We need to train people to learn the technology, how to use the new technology as well.
我们需要培训人们学习技术，以及如何运用新技术。

399
00:28:04,119 --> 00:28:12,119
Okay. It's certainly a very big topic. We can't cover all, but I think we're trying to scratch the surface at least.
好的。这确实是一个非常大的话题。我们无法面面俱到，但我想我们至少触及了表面。

400
00:28:12,119 --> 00:28:18,119
Thank you so much, Professor He Ping, Associate Dean of the School of Economics and Management at Tsinghua University.
非常感谢何平教授，清华大学经济管理学院副院长。

401
00:28:18,119 --> 00:28:19,619
Thank you.
谢谢。

402
00:28:25,119 --> 00:28:30,119
And that's it for this edition of The Point with me, Li Jing, coming to you from Beijing.
以上就是本期由我李静在北京为您带来的《锐评》。

403
00:28:30,119 --> 00:28:33,119
On behalf of the whole team, thank you for watching. You've got The Point.
代表整个团队，感谢大家的收看。这就是《锐评》。

404
00:28:42,119 --> 00:28:53,119
Making sense of the overwhelming wave of information means cutting through the noise to shine a light on the heart of the story
在信息洪流中理清头绪，意味着要穿透噪音，照亮故事的核心，

405
00:28:53,119 --> 00:28:56,119
and making room for new perspectives.
并为新的视角腾出空间。

406
00:28:56,119 --> 00:29:02,119
True understanding means the ability to see events from more than one side.
真正的理解意味着能够从多个角度看待事件。

407
00:29:02,119 --> 00:29:05,119
I'm Li Jing, and this is The Point.
我是李静，这里是《锐评》。

408
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:14,119
Thank you.
谢谢。

409
00:29:42,119 --> 00:29:44,119
Thank you.
谢谢。
